hadiths[5]{hadithnumber,text}:
"744","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), he (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Nothing of prophethood remains except the righteous servant's dream, and it is one forty-sixth part of prophethood."
"745","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever saw me in a dream has indeed seen me, for Satan cannot take my form."" Kulayb says: I narrated this hadith to Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) and I said: Indeed, I have seen the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) in a dream. So he said: Do you remember the martyrdom of Hasan bin Ali (may Allah be pleased with them both)? I said: Yes, by Allah! I even remember his gait. Then he said: Indeed, Hasan (may Allah be pleased with him) resembled the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him)."
"746","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever deliberately lies about me, let him take his place in Hell."" When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) mentioned this, he said: ""A righteous man's dream is one forty-sixth part of prophethood."
"747","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), he (peace be upon him) said: ""A good dream is from Allah, while a bad dream is from Satan. When any of you sees something he dislikes, he should spit three times to his left and not mention it, for it cannot harm him."
"748","Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) narrated: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) lifted the curtain while the people (the noble Companions, may Allah be pleased with them) were standing in rows behind Sayyiduna Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him), so he (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Of the glad tidings of Prophethood, only good/righteous dreams remain, which a Muslim sees or which are shown to him."" Then he said: ""Listen! I have been forbidden from reciting the Qur'an while in the state of bowing or prostration. As for bowing, glorify the greatness of your Lord in it, and as for prostration, make abundant supplication in it, for it is more likely that your supplications will be answered."
